WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.373
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.673 --> 00:00:09.013
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:15.379
Unit thirty-four: Formal Prepositional Phrases. Today you will write with formal fixed expressions.

4
00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:18.529
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.456
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:24.480
In terms of.

7
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:28.400
In terms of means regarding a particular aspect.

8
00:00:29.017 --> 00:00:31.167
In terms of cost, it's cheap.

9
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.296
Your turn. Say: In terms of.

10
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.285
In terms of.

11
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:40.086
With regard to.

12
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:42.851
With regard to means concerning.

13
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.275
With regard to your request...

14
00:00:45.883 --> 00:00:48.803
Your turn. Say: With regard to.

15
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:53.074
With regard to.

16
00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:54.899
On behalf of.

17
00:00:55.883 --> 00:00:58.440
On behalf of means representing someone.

18
00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.632
On behalf of the team...

19
00:01:01.217 --> 00:01:04.032
Your turn. Say: On behalf of.

20
00:01:06.867 --> 00:01:08.123
On behalf of.

21
00:01:08.883 --> 00:01:10.001
In accordance with.

22
00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:13.190
In accordance with means following a rule.

23
00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:15.423
In accordance with the law.

24
00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:18.530
Your turn. Say: In accordance with.

25
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:22.670
In accordance with.

26
00:01:23.417 --> 00:01:24.638
As a result of.

27
00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.951
As a result of means because of.

28
00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.190
As a result of the storm...

29
00:01:30.783 --> 00:01:33.865
Your turn. Say: As a result of.

30
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.038
As a result of.

31
00:01:38.783 --> 00:01:39.970
In spite of.

32
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:42.693
In spite of means despite.

33
00:01:43.283 --> 00:01:44.749
In spite of the rain...

34
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.933
Your turn. Say: In spite of.

35
00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:51.919
In spite of.

36
00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:53.742
By means of.

37
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.401
By means of means using.

38
00:01:57.017 --> 00:01:58.296
By means of a loan.

39
00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:01.652
Your turn. Say: By means of.

40
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.675
By means of.

41
00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:07.453
Due to.

42
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.008
Due to means because of.

43
00:02:10.617 --> 00:02:11.745
Due to the storm...

44
00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:14.677
Your turn. Say: Due to.

45
00:02:17.533 --> 00:02:18.418
Due to.

46
00:02:19.233 --> 00:02:22.524
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.383 --> 00:02:26.288
Visal, start a formal sentence with with regard to.

48
00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:35.492
With regard to your request, we will reply soon. Formal prepositional phrases are common in letters, reports and academic writing.

49
00:02:36.583 --> 00:02:37.584
Give me more.

50
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:50.931
In terms of cost, this plan is cheaper. On behalf of the team, I thank you. The work was done in accordance with the regulations. The road is closed as a result of the storm.

51
00:02:52.017 --> 00:02:53.204
How do we use them?

52
00:02:54.317 --> 00:03:09.255
After the phrase, use a noun or -ing form, never a full clause: due to the delay, not due to the train was late. In spite of is followed by a noun or -ing. Choose formal phrases only for formal writing.

53
00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.807
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:16.821
Grammar focus: Formal prepositional phrases plus noun and -ing.

55
00:03:17.121 --> 00:03:18.284
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.983 --> 00:03:21.830
With regard to your request, we will reply soon.

57
00:03:22.717 --> 00:03:25.366
As a result of the storm, the road is closed.

58
00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.213
In terms of cost, this plan is cheaper.

59
00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:37.321
Formal phrases (with regard to, in terms of, due to, as a result of) are followed by a noun or -ing, not by a full clause.

60
00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:41.328
Be careful! Don't say: Due to the train was late.

61
00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.777
Say: Due to the train's delay.

62
00:03:46.077 --> 00:03:47.659
Use a noun phrase.

63
00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:51.119
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:51.933 --> 00:03:53.201
Formal Phrases.

65
00:03:53.501 --> 00:03:57.010
With regard to your request, we will reply next week.

66
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.195
In terms of cost, this plan is much cheaper.

67
00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.768
On behalf of the whole team, I thank you.

68
00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:08.637
As a result of the storm, the road is closed.

69
00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:12.597
The work was done in accordance with local regulations.

70
00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:17.470
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.317 --> 00:04:20.595
blank your letter, we will reply soon.

72
00:04:20.895 --> 00:04:24.757
A, With regard to. B, In order. C, Because.

73
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.497
The answer is A: With regard to.

74
00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.882
The match was cancelled blank the rain.

75
00:04:34.182 --> 00:04:37.487
A, due to. B, because. C, so.

76
00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:43.428
The answer is A: due to.

77
00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:45.828
Which is correct?

78
00:04:46.128 --> 00:04:52.429
A, Due to the train was late, I left.. B, Due to the delay, I left.. C, Due to delay, I leaving..

79
00:04:55.967 --> 00:04:59.046
The answer is B: Due to the delay, I left..

80
00:05:00.183 --> 00:05:01.986
'On behalf of' means blank.

81
00:05:02.286 --> 00:05:06.055
A, representing. B, opposing. C, preventing.

82
00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.064
The answer is A: representing.

83
00:05:13.217 --> 00:05:15.472
According to the reading, what is closed?

84
00:05:15.772 --> 00:05:19.866
A, the road. B, the school. C, the bridge.

85
00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.423
The answer is A: the road.

86
00:05:26.633 --> 00:05:30.296
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:33.997
Write a formal sentence starting with 'With regard to…'.

88
00:05:42.783 --> 00:05:44.644
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:56.875
With regard to your application, we are pleased to offer you an interview. In terms of qualifications, you meet the requirements. I use formal phrases because this is a professional letter.

90
00:05:57.175 --> 00:05:58.803
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:59.717 --> 00:06:04.865
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and formal prepositional phrases plus noun and -ing.

92
00:06:05.165 --> 00:06:10.708
Today's value is eloquence. Choose your words with care, and speak to persuade honestly.

93
00:06:11.008 --> 00:06:13.870
See you in Unit thirty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.892
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

